# Audit Rules: Rust Crate Structure

## Rule S-01 â€” No orphan .rs files outside src/

```yaml
rule:    S-01
title:   "All .rs module files MUST reside in crate/src/"
severity: P0_COMPILE_BLOCKER
rationale: |
  Cargo resolves lib root as src/lib.rs by default.
  .rs files in crate root (coge/mod.rs, coge/infer.rs) are
  INVISIBLE to compiler â€” they do not get compiled.

violation_example:
  bad:
    - "coge/mod.rs      (root)"
    - "coge/infer.rs    (root)"
    - "coge/lora.rs     (root)"
    - "coge/run.rs      (root)"
  good:
    - "coge/src/lib.rs"
    - "coge/src/infer.rs"
    - "coge/src/lora.rs"
    - "coge/src/run.rs"

current_violation: "engine/hace/brain/coge/ â€” 4 orphan files"
fix: "mv coge/mod.rs coge/src/lib.rs; mv coge/{infer,lora,run}.rs coge/src/"
```

## Rule S-02 â€” Every crate directory MUST have Cargo.toml

```yaml
rule:    S-02
title:   "Crate directory without Cargo.toml cannot be workspace member"
severity: P0_COMPILE_BLOCKER

violation_example:
  bad:
    - "brain/src/  (has .rs files, no Cargo.toml)"
    - "brain/io/   (has .rs files, no Cargo.toml)"
  good:
    - "brain/base/Cargo.toml  exists"
    - "brain/master/Cargo.toml exists"

current_violations:
  brain_src: "engine/hace/brain/src/ â€” no Cargo.toml, 7 .rs files orphaned"
  brain_io:  "engine/hace/brain/io/ â€” no Cargo.toml, 7 .rs files orphaned"

fix_brain_src: |
  DECISION (CSA): DELETE brain/src/ entirely.
  Rationale: ops duplicated in fem/hacedle/src/ops/ (canonical source).
  attention.rs fix unverifiable while orphaned.
  If attention fix is needed: cherry-pick into hacedle/ops/attention.rs.

fix_brain_io: |
  DECISION (CSA): Use engine/hace/io/ (already exists, has RAC variants).
  brain/io/ files duplicate io/rac* â€” delete and import hace-io crate.
```

## Rule S-03 â€” No silent stubs (fn f() -> T { T::default() })

```yaml
rule:    S-03
title:   "Stub functions MUST emit explicit warn! or return typed error, not silent default"
severity: P1_QUALITY

rationale: |
  BrainMasterRuntime::execute() returning SioOutcome::default() silently
  causes 'success' responses with empty data â€” harder to debug than Err.

required_pattern: |
  // WRONG:
  pub fn execute(&self, sio: RuntimeSio) -> Result<SioOutcome, &'static str> {
      Ok(SioOutcome::default())  // silent stub
  }

  // CORRECT (E4 stub):
  pub fn execute(&self, sio: RuntimeSio) -> Result<SioOutcome, BrainError> {
      Err(BrainError::ReasonFailed {
          msg: "InferenceEngine not yet wired (GAP-T1)".to_string()
      })
  }

  // CORRECT (E4 pass-through with log):
  pub fn execute(&self, sio: RuntimeSio) -> Result<SioOutcome, BrainError> {
      log::warn!("brain::execute: falling back to AlgoParticle (CE not loaded)");
      self.algo_fallback(sio)
  }

current_violations:
  - "brain/master/src/lib.rs::execute() -> Ok(SioOutcome::default())"
  - "brain/master/src/inference/engine.rs::infer() stub"
  - "brain/runtime/src/dispatcher.rs::dispatch() -> let _ = session"
```

## Rule S-04 â€” No hardcoded model metadata

```yaml
rule:    S-04
title:   "Model architecture/tensor counts MUST NOT be hardcoded"
severity: P1_CORRECTNESS

violation_example:
  bad: |
    // brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs
    fn verify(&self, _path: &str) -> GgufInfo {
        GgufInfo { architecture: "qwen2".into(), tensors: 291 }
    }
  good: |
    fn verify(&self, path: &str) -> Result<GgufInfo, GgufError> {
        let loader = GgufLoaderStd::open(path)?;
        Ok(GgufInfo::from_header(&loader.header))
    }

current_violation: "brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs (pre-fix)"
```

## Rule S-05 â€” hacedle ops are canonical, no reimplementation

```yaml
rule:    S-05
title:   "Do not reimplement ops that exist in fem/hacedle/src/ops/ or x/loader/gguf/"
severity: P0_REUSE_VIOLATION

canonical_sources:
  gguf_parsing:  "fem/hacedle/src/x/loader/gguf/loader_std.rs"
  tensor_index:  "fem/hacedle/src/x/loader/gguf/tensor_index.rs"
  rmsnorm:       "fem/hacedle/src/ops/rmsnorm.rs"
  rope:          "fem/hacedle/src/ops/rope.rs"
  attention_ops: "fem/hacedle/src/ops/attention.rs"
  silu:          "fem/hacedle/src/ops/silu.rs"
  matmul:        "fem/hacedle/src/ops/matmul.rs  (if added)"
  dequant_q4k:   "fem/hacedle/src/x/loader/dequant/q4_k.rs"
  candle_layer:  "fem/hacedle/src/x/provider/candle/layer.rs"
  candle_lmhead: "fem/hacedle/src/x/provider/candle/lmhead.rs"

violation_detection: |
  audit/scripts/duplication_check.py scans brain/master/src for
  any re-implementation of the above. Raises P0 if found.
```
